The meta-d’ model
We can directly compare sensitivityfor Type I and Type II decisions:





\[
\begin{align*}
M &= \frac{\textrm{meta-}d'}{d'}
\end{align*}
\]


metacognitive sensitivity Type I sensitivity

metacognitiveefficiency



\(M\)-ratio is an independent measure of  the relationship between confidence and accuracy

hmetad: an R package for hierarchical Bayesian modeling of confidence ratings










## fit a multilevel meta-d' model
m &lt;- fit_metad(
  bf(
    N ~ 1 + (1 | participant),
    dprime ~ 1 + (1 | participant),
    c ~ 1 + (1 | participant),
    metac2zero1diff ~ 1 + (1 | participant),
    metac2one1diff ~ 1 + (1 | participant)
  ), data=d, ...
)

## compute meta-delta by participant
d |&gt;
  distinct(participant) |&gt;
  add_metacognitive_bias_draws(m) |&gt;
  median_qi()
